{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0730"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge earth-space/geology","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/earth-space__geology.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",1012],["+","The southernmost of them all stands on Ross Island, off the coast of Antarctica. Mount Erebus, 3,792 metres high, is the world's southernmost active volcano and one of the few on Earth with a lava lake, which has bubbled in its summit crater since at least the early 1970s. The British explorer James Clark Ross saw it erupting on 27 January 1841 and named it after his ship, HMS Erebus; a party from Ernest Shackleton's Nimrod expedition first reached its crater rim on 10 March 1908.\n\n"],["=",99],["+","\n| Erebus | Ross Island (Antarctica) | 3,792 m |"]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",958],["+","Der südlichste von allen steht auf der Ross-Insel vor der Küste von Antarktika. Der 3.792 Meter hohe Mount Erebus ist der südlichste aktive Vulkan der Welt und einer der wenigen auf der Erde mit einem Lavasee, der seit mindestens Anfang der 1970er-Jahre in seinem Gipfelkrater brodelt. Der britische Entdecker James Clark Ross sah ihn am 27. Januar 1841 ausbrechen und benannte ihn nach seinem Schiff, der HMS Erebus; eine Gruppe von Ernest Shackletons Nimrod-Expedition erreichte am 10. März 1908 erstmals seinen Kraterrand.\n\n"],["=",99],["+","\n| Erebus | Ross-Insel (Antarktika) | 3.792 m |"]]}]},
{"seq":3,"at":"2026-10-21","kind":"corrected","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0730"},"reason":"a0730 body: Mauna Loa \"34 eruptions\" → \"more than 30\"; Etna height \"about 3,350 m\" → \"about 3,400 m\" (3,403 m in 2024); Fuji \"at least sixteen eruptions since 781\" (unverified) → \"many times in recorded history\", Hōei eruption named; Eyjafjallajökull and Erebus sentences now name Iceland / Antarctica — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Etna , https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Fuji","by":"enrich batch 038","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-enrich/enrich-report/a2159-a0850.md","sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Etna"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Fuji"}]},
